      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>A card&#39;s effect will only stay in effect after the card is gone if the effect has a specific duration which hasn&#39;t been met yet. For example, I think the power on Ra&#39;s Flesh of the Sun God makes all heroes immune to fire until the start of Ra&#39;s next turn. If Ra used that power on his turn but was then incapacitated, everyone would still be immune to fire until Ra&#39;s next turn came around. The same goes for effects caused by a target (such as Akash&#39;Bhuta&#39;s Ensnaring Brambles) if the target is destroyed between turns.</p>",
