    {
      "id": 83723,
      "name": "Envisioner",
      "username": "Envisioner",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2013-12-05T22:40:51.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>A reason for Ground Pound to be worded the way it does is Omnitron-X's Timeshift power, which puts the top card of a deck directly into play; if you TS a Groundpound, you've wasted your power unless Haka has the cards to discard.&nbsp; (Combine this with his Haka cards, Punish the Weak, and the multiple copies of Mere and Taiaha, and Haka is generally not a good target for Timeshift.)&nbsp; Similar things happen if you fight in Atlantis, where the Font of Power plays the top card of everyone's deck, or against the Ennead if you kill Set early (not generally recommended, by the way).&nbsp; All of these can cause Haka to play Ground Pound even if he's not quite ready to.</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:06:53.184Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
