      "username": "NAL0781",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/nal0781/{size}/2041_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-12-07T03:24:06.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Foote\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/48/1877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Foote:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>McBehrer wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Killing Set first is my FAVORITE way of beating the Ennead. Just throwing that out there.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nKilling Set early is usually my biggest mistake when playing on advanced. At least it always feels that way. They always happen to crush me the exact turn after Set dies every. single. time.&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>The best way for me to beat the Ennead is for Set to remain under the Shrine for the duration of the match!</p>",
